  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Da» with the present indicative",
     "texto": [
      "It corresponds to the English «have been + -ing» and «for»: **Vivo qui da tre anni** (I've been living here for three years); **Studio l'italiano da sei mesi** (I've been studying Italian for six months).",
      "Careful! The past isn't used, because the action is still open and ongoing at the moment of speaking."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking about duration",
     "texto": [
      "To ask how long an ongoing action has lasted, you say **Da quanto tempo...?**: **Da quanto tempo abiti a Roma?** (How long have you been living in Rome?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
